    <h2>1. Why Navbar & Footer Matter Most</h2>
    <p>Navbar is the <b>first thing</b> user sees. Footer is the <b>last thing</b> user sees. If navbar is confusing, user leaves in 3 seconds. If footer has no contact, user cannot hire you.</p>
    <p>Every page on a website shares the SAME navbar and SAME footer. You build them once, copy to all pages. That is why professionals master these two first. This website - LearnHTMLCSSJS.com - also uses the same navbar + footer on all 50 lessons.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Rule:</b> Navbar = Where can I go? Footer = How can I contact you + Where is everything? If user cannot answer these in 3 seconds, your navbar/footer failed.</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - Full Navbar + Footer - Try It</h2>
    <p>Try: Hover Services for dropdown, click hamburger on mobile, click links for active color, scroll for sticky:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
